  "riskClass": "high",
  "title": "inventory-service getAllStockBalancesForStore returns unbounded result set without pagination or LIMIT clause",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: db_queries. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The `getAllStockBalancesForStore` function (lines 174-187) executes `SELECT ... FROM inventory.stock_balances WHERE store_id = $1 ORDER BY product_id` with NO LIMIT clause. This query is called from the route GET /stores/:storeId/inventory (inventory.ts line 62-67) which also applies no pagination. A store with 10,000+ products would return all stock balances in a single response, causing: (1) memory pressure on the Node.js process, (2) large response payload transferred over the network, (3) slow query on large tables. The route also doesn't validate or cap the user-supplied `limit` parameter for `/recent` (line 91: `parseInt(req.query.limit as string, 10) || 100`) — a user could pass `limit=999999`.",
